---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab library load documents (`event.category`
  `library`) per window, host, library, and loading process. Other documents
  pass through unchanged.

  The first load of every library by a process executable in a window passes
  through immediately and unchanged, with the process ID. Further loads of
  the library by the same executable in the same window are repeats: when the
  window closes, one summary document stands for them, and a key without
  repeats gets no summary. A summary stays an ECS library document.
  `event.start` and `event.end` hold the times of the first and last repeat,
  `event.duration` the time between them in nanoseconds, and `@timestamp`
  equals `event.start`. ECS has no field for the number of events that a
  document stands for, so `tenzir.count` holds the number of repeats, which
  excludes the first load. Only summaries have `tenzir.count`.

  The key covers the whole `dll` record, with its path, hashes, code
  signature, and PE header, and `file.size`, so another binary at the same
  path gets its own summary. It also covers the loading process by its
  executable (`process.executable`), so a library that an unusual process
  loads gets a first occurrence of its own. The process ID of the loading
  process appears only if all repeats came from the same one.

  The summary takes the host, agent, and organization from the first document
  of the host with the same event kind and type in the window.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing, the memory it needs, and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1h
      description: Width of the deduplication windows, in processing and event
        time.
---

// `$window` names the argument only outside the `window` block.
if event.category?.first() == "library" {
  _host = host?.id? else agent?.id? else host?.hostname?
  _time = time(this["@timestamp"]?)
  _bucket = _time.floor($window)
  // Every group key and aggregate costs memory per summary. The summaries
  // therefore group by digests: `_ids` covers the values that few documents
  // of a host share, and `_library` the library, which is the same on many
  // hosts. The values behind the digests come from one context record per
  // host and `_ids` and one record per `_library`. The host, agent, and
  // organization come from the first document of the context.
  _ids = hash_xxh3([host?.id?, host?.hostname?, agent?.id?, agent?.name?,
    event?.kind?, event?.type?])
  _library = hash_md5([dll?, file?])
  window size=$window {
    // The digest covers the same keys as the summary below. Keep both lists
    // identical, so that every summary belongs to one first occurrence.
    _key = hash_md5([_host, _bucket, _ids, _library, process?.executable?])
    summarize _key, _seen=count(), options={mode: "cumulative"}
    if _seen == 1 {
      drop _key, _host, _time, _bucket, _ids, _library, _seen
    } else {
      fork_merge {
        summarize _host, _bucket, _ids, _library, process?.executable?,
          count=count(), start=min(_time), end=max(_time),
          _pid_min=min(process?.pid?), _pid_max=max(process?.pid?),
          _pid_count=count(process?.pid?)
      }, {
        summarize _host, _ids, _context=first({
          agent: agent?,
          ecs: ecs?,
          kind: event?.kind?,
          type: event?.type?,
          host: host?,
          organization: organization?,
        })
      }, {
        summarize _library, _object=first({dll: dll?, file: file?})
      }
      // Each context and library record sorts before the summaries that it
      // belongs to, so a running `first` hands it to each of them.
      sort _host?, _ids?, _context? == null
      summarize _host?, _ids?, _ctx=first(_context?),
        options={mode: "cumulative"}
      sort _library?, _object? == null
      summarize _library?, _lib=first(_object?),
        options={mode: "cumulative"}
      where _context? == null and _object? == null
      this = {
        "@timestamp": start,
        agent: _ctx.agent,
        dll: _lib.dll,
        ecs: _ctx.ecs,
        event: {
          category: ["library"],
          kind: _ctx.kind,
          type: _ctx.type,
          start: start,
          end: end,
          duration: int((end - start) / 1ns),
        },
        file: _lib.file,
        host: _ctx.host,
        organization: _ctx.organization,
        process: {
          executable: process.executable,
          pid: _pid_min
            if _pid_min == _pid_max and _pid_count == count else null,
        },
        tenzir: {count: count},
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
